Featuring a sleek, dark metallic silver and charcoal frame, "Romeo" retained the oversized circular chest Arc Reactor aperture found on heavy artillery suits. Tony designed this armor to test rapid energy-transfer subroutines, allowing the suit to charge its offensive weapons—or transfer energy to surrounding systems and allies—at double the speed of standard armors without suffering internal thermal spikes.

In Iron Man 3, Mark XXXII flies in with the Iron Legion during the House Party Protocol at the Norco oil rig, engaging Extremis soldiers in air-to-ground skirmishes before being destroyed in the final "Clean Slate" detonation order.
